  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/700AE3">Definition <span data-tag="700AE3">7.3.1.4</span>.</a>proper!morphism of $\infty $-topoi Let $p_{\ast }: \calX \rightarrow \calY $ be a geometric morphism of $\infty $-topoi. We will say that $p_{\ast }$ is <em>proper</em> if the following condition is satisfied: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(\ast )$"><p>
For every Cartesian rectangle 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { \calX '' \ar [d] \ar [r] &amp;  \calX ' \ar [d] \ar [r] &amp;  \calX \ar [d]^{p_{\ast }} \\ \calY '' \ar [r] &amp;  \calY ' \ar [r] &amp;  \calY } \]
</div>
<p>
 of $\infty $-topoi, the left square is left adjointable. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
